Q: how to serialize jobs in BullMQ A: <p>i solved this by using parentJobId , by adding jobs in the same queue with same parentJobId from child worker</p>
<p>so flow queue and child queue should be same and jobId of the flow should be used to add more children dynamically in the same queue</p>
<p>but i am not sure if this is the right way but its working for me in production:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const parentJobId = '&lt;some_unique_id_shared_by_parent_and_children&gt;'

await flowProducer.add({
  name: &quot;import-data&quot;,
  queueName: &quot;imports&quot;,
  opts: { 
    jobId: parentJobId
  },
  children: [
    {
      name: &quot;fetch-page&quot;,
      queueName: &quot;imports&quot;,
      data: {
        pageToken: null,
        parentJobId,
      },
    },
  ],
});
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const result = await fetchPage(job.data.pageToken);

if (result.nextPageToken) {
  await queue.add(
    &quot;fetch-page&quot;,
    {
      pageToken: result.nextPageToken,
      parentJobId,
    },
    {
      parent: {
        id: parentJobId,
        queue: &quot;bull:imports&quot;,
      },
    }
  );
}

</code></pre>
<p>you can check my question on this to get more details:
<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79987711/bullmq-flow-is-it-supported-to-dynamically-add-child-jobs-to-an-existing-parent">BullMQ Flow: Is it supported to dynamically add child jobs to an existing parent while processing?</a></p>
